- **Where the Frame Stops Working:** it said Druski "hasn't engaged a single named critic on substance," but he answered the Parham lawsuit with phone records. It now reads "outside the Parham case."
- **Loose thread closed:** the childhood section says he's "still running that play in larger rooms," and nothing ever paid that off. One clause in the Whiteface section now links the "AM I CANCELLED?" post and the deleted "too far" post back to the "I'm just joking" habit.

**Transition fixes (5):**
- Depression → Roast: "Often the laugh is at his own expense." This picks up "every laugh he chases" and gives "the move" something to point to.
- Roast → Whiteface: the section now ends on "from a parent or a senator, the mechanism shuts off," which sets up the next two sections.
- Whiteface → Mafiathon: "Before the senator, there was a mother." This marks the jump from 2026 back to 2024.
- Under Fire → Netflix: "He had paid for that brand himself." This picks up "the brand" from the Parham section's closing line.
- Frame section → What's Next: "keeps cashing, even in rooms he doesn't run." The page no longer ends twice.

**Flow within sections (4):**
- Childhood: moved the mother's "His discipline is his key" to the end of the section, so the timeline doesn't jump to 2025 and back.
- Roast: moved the Bieber lines up so "works for the same reason" points at the right sentence.
- Diagnosis: cut the second mention of the streaming rejection.
- Where the Frame Stops Working: cut its restatement of the inside/outside-the-circle point, which the Roast section now makes.

**Cuts to pay for the bridges:** "The tension escalated," "Most people would have fallen in line," "most people would have been mortified."

